{"created": "2025-07-11T15:15:03.033412+00:00", "modified": "2025-07-11T15:15:04.129714+00:00", "id": 15864525, "conceptrecid": "15864524", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15864525", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.15864524", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15864525", "metadata": {"title": "Dataset for Beyond Double-Double Theory: n-Directional Stacking Sequence Optimisation in Composite Laminates", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.15864525", "publication_date": "2025-07-11", "description": "<p>Authors: Jos&eacute; Humberto S. Almeida Jr., Emilia Balonek, Saullo G. P. Castro<br>Contact: Saullo G. P. Castro<br>Date: 11/July/2025<br>Affiliation: Department of Mechanical Engineering, LUT University; Department of Aerospace Structures and Materials, Delft University of Technology<br>Paper Title: 'Beyond Double-Double Theory: n-Directional Stacking Sequence Optimisation in Composite Laminates'<br>Dependencies: numpy, scipy, pymoo, composites, bfscplate2d</p>\n<h1>1. OVERVIEW</h1>\n<p>One code that was created for optimization of 48 plies laminate has four versions.<br>Each version was used to perform optimization for varying number of Double-Double (DD) laminates:<br>a) D_Case1 &ndash; code for n-D layout which allows one D<br>b) DD_Case1 &ndash; code for n-D layout which allows two D's<br>c) DDD_Case1 &ndash; code for n-D layout which allows three D's<br>d) DDDD_Case1 &ndash; code for n-D layout which allows four D's</p>\n<p>Then, each code from these mentioned above has its own four version depending on the type<br>of loading chosen and whether the optimisation needs to be performed using Genetic Alghorithm (GA) or not:<br>i) pymoo - code considered biaxial loading and was performed using stiffness matching approach<br>ii) pymoo_free - code considered biaxial loading and was performed using GA<br>iii) pymoo_load - code considered uniaxial loading and was performed using stiffness matching approach<br>iv) pymoo_uniaxial_free - code considered uniaxial loading and was performed using GA</p>\n<h1>2. DESCRIPTION</h1>\n<p>This file describes the codes used to generate the results in the paper.<br>Here, the Python codes perform stacking sequence optimization of composite laminates using a Double-Double (DD) laminate configuration.&nbsp;<br>The objective is to maximize structural performance under different types of loading and obtain buckling and failure loads.</p>\n<h1>3. KEY FEATURES</h1>\n<p>- Five configurations of plate dimensions 'a' and 'b' were tested giving following aspect ratios: 0.5, 1, 2, 3, and 4. &nbsp;<br>- Biaxial in-plane loading: 'Nxx = 1.0 lb/in', 'Nyy = 0.5 lb/in' or uniaxial in-plane loading: 'Nxx = 1.0 lb/in', 'Nyy = 0 lb/in'<br>- Stiffness matching optimization or Genetic Algorithm (GA) approach<br>- Constraints set are the same througt all files: symmetric and balanced laminate</p>\n<h1>4. KEY OPERATIONS&nbsp;</h1>\n<p>a) 'objective' function is based on stiffness matching to generate n-D layups with equivalent in-plane stiffness to&nbsp;<br>reference laminates under biaxial and uniaxial compressive loading</p>\n<p>b) 'objective_free' function is based on GA and explores the optimum stacking sequences that maximise&nbsp;<br>buckling resistance and delay failure onset</p>\n<h1>5. OUTPUTS</h1>\n<p>- Optimal stacking sequence (in degrees)<br>- '&lambda;_cb' buckling load (in Newtons)<br>- '&lambda;_cs' failure load (in Newtons)</p>\n<h1>6. RUNNING PROCEDURE OF EACH CODE</h1>\n<p>1. Open environment with Python 3.11</p>\n<p>2. Install required packages by using \"pip install numpy scipy pymoo composites bfscplate2d\" command</p>\n<p>3. Define parameters such as aspect ratio</p>\n<p>4. Run the script</p>\n<p>5. Review output&nbsp;</p>\n<h1>7. REFERENCE</h1>\n<p>Haftka, R. T. (1993). Optimization of laminate stacking sequence for buckling or strength. AIAA Journal, 31(5), 921&ndash;922.</p>\n<h1>8. NOTES</h1>\n<p>- All experiments were run on Windows 10.<br>- These codes were tested with Python 3.11 version.<br>- These codes are for research purposes and were developed for this paper.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Almeida Jr, Humberto", "affiliation": "Lappeenranta-Lahti University of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0002-9408-7674"}, {"name": "Balonek, Emilia", "affiliation": "Lappeenranta-Lahti University of Technology"}, {"name": "G. P. Castro, Saullo", "affiliation": "Delft University of Technology", "orcid": "0000-0001-9711-0991"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "mit-license"}, "communities": [{"id": "crashprooflab"}], "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "15864524"}}]}}, "title": "Dataset for Beyond Double-Double Theory: n-Directional Stacking Sequence Optimisation in Composite Laminates", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15864525", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15864525", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15864525?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15864525", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15864525", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.15864525", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15864525/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15864524", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/15864524", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15864524", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.15864524", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:15864525/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:15864525/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15864525/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15864525/media-files", "archive": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15864525/files-archive", "archive_media": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15864525/media-files-archive", "latest": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/15864525/versions/latest", "latest